(1576027, 204922, 11800, '<td valign="top">.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-29 17:20:53.</i></td>', '.', '2005-07-31 15:45:27.000000', '2005-09-29 18:20:53.000000', 0),
(1576590, 205860, 15711, '<td valign="top">I think this might have been just a tad bit too busy.  Maybe it would have been more effective if you just zoomed in on one leaf and it''s texture were the focus, instead of the texture of it against the other leaves mixed in with all of the lighting and shadow.  When you throw all of that into the mix, it busies it up too much to make the impact I think you were seeking.  Does that make sense??  Hope this is helpful.  The overall idea is a good one.</td>', 'I think this might have been just a tad bit too busy.  Maybe it would have been more effective if you just zoomed in on one leaf and it''s texture were the focus, instead of the texture of it against the other leaves mixed in with all of the lighting and shadow.  When you throw all of that into the mix, it busies it up too much to make the impact I think you were seeking.  Does that make sense??  Hope this is helpful.  The overall idea is a good one.', '2005-07-31 22:49:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576596, 206564, 15711, '<td valign="top">I think the look you obtain when you sharpen something after the fact is never as good as if it were crystal clear to begin with.  I have found that more times than I care to mention.  Since you had asked in the forum, I thought I''d just respond this way. <br/> <br/>I love the single claw and the statement it makes as sort of an "alien" type prehistoric being, but to me it is still slightly out of focus.The lighting and composition is excellent  I hope this is helpful.</td>', 'I think the look you obtain when you sharpen something after the fact is never as good as if it were crystal clear to begin with.  I have found that more times than I care to mention.  Since you had asked in the forum, I thought I''d just respond this way.  I love the single claw and the statement it makes as sort of an "alien" type prehistoric being, but to me it is still slightly out of focus.The lighting and composition is excellent  I hope this is helpful.', '2005-07-31 22:52:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576620, 204745, 15711, '<td valign="top">I did not comment on this during the Texture voting and I should have.  The composition is good and I like the warm tones of the eggs against the gray/black tones of the counter. It didn''t totally knock me out, but it wasn''t a bad photo at all.  I gave it a 6 and had it been in a different challenge like perhaps "color variations" or "Three," I might have given it a 7 or 8.</td>', 'I did not comment on this during the Texture voting and I should have.  The composition is good and I like the warm tones of the eggs against the gray/black tones of the counter. It didn''t totally knock me out, but it wasn''t a bad photo at all.  I gave it a 6 and had it been in a different challenge like perhaps "color variations" or "Three," I might have given it a 7 or 8.', '2005-07-31 23:02:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576633, 206468, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like this photograph. I voted but failed to comment during the challenge as there were soooo many.  Since I vote on every single photo, I don''t always have the time to comment.  I like the title as it depicts a less religious take on the thorn crown, yet it is something familiar to most and it makes us take a second look.  My only critique might be one of perhaps to tone down the bright of the clouds just a smidge. I had given this a 7 during the voting process.</td>', 'I like this photograph. I voted but failed to comment during the challenge as there were soooo many.  Since I vote on every single photo, I don''t always have the time to comment.  I like the title as it depicts a less religious take on the thorn crown, yet it is something familiar to most and it makes us take a second look.  My only critique might be one of perhaps to tone down the bright of the clouds just a smidge. I had given this a 7 during the voting process.', '2005-07-31 23:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576642, 203618, 15711, '<td valign="top">There''s something about faces and when shot well, they always get a high score.  I had given this a 9 and don''t know why I didn''t comment on it.  I think the lighting and the composition is really artfully done, considering it''s a reptile. LOL</td>', 'There''s something about faces and when shot well, they always get a high score.  I had given this a 9 and don''t know why I didn''t comment on it.  I think the lighting and the composition is really artfully done, considering it''s a reptile. LOL', '2005-07-31 23:09:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576838, 204224, 32767, '<td valign="top">I gave you an 8 becuase you did a great job but at the end of the day it''s still just a bunch of Red Cabbage and Cabbage...no matter how red, will never set the world on fire.</td>', 'I gave you an 8 becuase you did a great job but at the end of the day it''s still just a bunch of Red Cabbage and Cabbage...no matter how red, will never set the world on fire.', '2005-08-01 00:43:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576842, 204224, 37234, '<td valign="top">The moment I saw this, that old Judas Priest song <b>immedately</b> got stuck in my brain.</td>', 'The moment I saw this, that old Judas Priest song immedately got stuck in my brain.', '2005-08-01 00:45:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576844, 205699, 1717, '<td valign="top">very cool shot!</td>', 'very cool shot!', '2005-08-01 00:45:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1576898, 205860, 35786, '<td valign="top">From a thread- just want to keep it w/ the image...<br/> <br/>The image is, first of all, not NEARLY as textural as you''d want it to be for this topic. It''s luminous, but it doesn''t really say "texture" to me. Compositionally, it''s divided vertically into an in-focus and an our-of-focus section more or less precisely on the vertical bisector of the image; that''s a very static composition. Fully half your image is out of focus, but it''s unfortunately rendering the same VALUE as the in-focus part (the leaves are lit the same), so it looks vaguely like sloppy work.<br/> <br/>Try making a selection of the in-focus leaf, invert the selection, and use levels to tone down everything but that leaf; I bet you''ll find that a distinct improvement. I realize that wouldn''t have been legal in this challenge, btw, but try it and watch what happens.<br/> <br/>Finally, the way the left arc of the subject leaf is truncated by the left edge of the image doesn''t feel right to me, especially inasmuch as there''s (as I mentioned) fully half the image out of focus on the right, an area that could easily have been eliminated to osme degree by panning the camera left on the subject leaf, so the ratio was more like 2/3, 1/3.<br/></td>', 'From a thread- just want to keep it w/ the image... The image is, first of all, not NEARLY as textural as you''d want it to be for this topic. It''s luminous, but it doesn''t really say "texture" to me. Compositionally, it''s divided vertically into an in-focus and an our-of-focus section more or less precisely on the vertical bisector of the image; that''s a very static composition. Fully half your image is out of focus, but it''s unfortunately rendering the same VALUE as the in-focus part (the leaves are lit the same), so it looks vaguely like sloppy work. Try making a selection of the in-focus leaf, invert the selection, and use levels to tone down everything but that leaf; I bet you''ll find that a distinct improvement. I realize that wouldn''t have been legal in this challenge, btw, but try it and watch what happens. Finally, the way the left arc of the subject leaf is truncated by the left edge of the image doesn''t feel right to me, especially inasmuch as there''s (as I mentioned) fully half the image out of focus on the right, an area that could easily have been eliminated to osme degree by panning the camera left on the subject leaf, so the ratio was more like 2/3, 1/3.', '2005-08-01 00:59:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1578154, 203692, 36679, '<td valign="top">It is an excellent lens, that Sigma 105 Macro. I have it for my D70 and love it. Very nice shot.</td>', 'It is an excellent lens, that Sigma 105 Macro. I have it for my D70 and love it. Very nice shot.', '2005-08-01 12:42:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1578251, 204956, 37673, '<td valign="top">Sajin , very nicely done. I would think this finished a lot better but just don''t understand some peoples voting. This photo has great evrything. The colors are great and the lighting was very creative. Focus tells me a lot about the texture of the subject and the composition is perfect. You may have gone a bit far on the contrast. It is starting to show a little noise but not too bad. I really like this photo.  Good job.</td>', 'Sajin , very nicely done. I would think this finished a lot better but just don''t understand some peoples voting. This photo has great evrything. The colors are great and the lighting was very creative. Focus tells me a lot about the texture of the subject and the composition is perfect. You may have gone a bit far on the contrast. It is starting to show a little noise but not too bad. I really like this photo.  Good job.', '2005-08-01 13:31:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1578473, 205677, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I do not think the overall composition works.  I think their are lots of textures to be had their but the light just does not seem to enhance any of them.  Probrably a closer crop on one selected element would have helped.  I do find the colors to be very vibrant and the red/burngundy contrasts nicely.</td>', 'From the Critique Club I do not think the overall composition works.  I think their are lots of textures to be had their but the light just does not seem to enhance any of them.  Probrably a closer crop on one selected element would have helped.  I do find the colors to be very vibrant and the red/burngundy contrasts nicely.', '2005-08-01 15:46:17.000000', NULL, 0),
