(1583828, 203951, 40584, '<td valign="top">Really brought out the theme is this one!  Didn''t realize how intricate that plant is.  Love the captured rain droplets on the background leaves.  Agree with other comment about color; could maybe enhance it a bit more.  Nice solid scores, too!</td>', 'Really brought out the theme is this one!  Didn''t realize how intricate that plant is.  Love the captured rain droplets on the background leaves.  Agree with other comment about color; could maybe enhance it a bit more.  Nice solid scores, too!', '2005-08-03 13:06:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1584108, 206145, 34659, '<td valign="top">First off let me say that I remember this image very well from the challenge.  It also reminded me of an Anne Geddes shot.  It has a lot of emotional appeal (everyone likes babies) and the softness and purity of the light really add to the overall mood.<br/> <br/>There are a couple of things I don''t think work as well as they could though.  The discoloration around the baby''s eye is a bit of a distraction (although I understand no spot editing allowed in basic challenge) and the crop didn''t really work for me.  I like the high key feel you''ve established and the bright white light, but I think a different crop might have served you better here - instead of close at the top, maybe close at the bottom?  Probably the biggest hit your score took though was because (as several other people have said), the actual textures in the image are too subtly displayed.<br/> <br/>I like it and think it''s really a good shot - just not necessarily represented the best it could have been for a Textures Challenge.<br/> <br/>Just my 2 cents...</td>', 'First off let me say that I remember this image very well from the challenge.  It also reminded me of an Anne Geddes shot.  It has a lot of emotional appeal (everyone likes babies) and the softness and purity of the light really add to the overall mood. There are a couple of things I don''t think work as well as they could though.  The discoloration around the baby''s eye is a bit of a distraction (although I understand no spot editing allowed in basic challenge) and the crop didn''t really work for me.  I like the high key feel you''ve established and the bright white light, but I think a different crop might have served you better here - instead of close at the top, maybe close at the bottom?  Probably the biggest hit your score took though was because (as several other people have said), the actual textures in the image are too subtly displayed. I like it and think it''s really a good shot - just not necessarily represented the best it could have been for a Textures Challenge. Just my 2 cents...', '2005-08-03 14:31:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1584698, 206468, 37234, '<td valign="top">I feel guilty not commenting on this one already. I gave it an 8 and think it''s a fabulous photo. I''m a bit of a sucker for B&amp;W and this one is very well done.</td>', 'I feel guilty not commenting on this one already. I gave it an 8 and think it''s a fabulous photo. I''m a bit of a sucker for B&W and this one is very well done.', '2005-08-03 18:07:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1585572, 203646, 14986, '<td valign="top">Wow..hard to believe this one came in so low.  I think it''s just an excellent shot.  Good exposure, good focus and use of b/w and nice casual pose of the subject.  I like the rather dark contrast and tend to use that a bit more myself.  I think it adds some drama to a shot. It''s done really well here without overdoing it.<br/> <br/>The only thing I can see to do differently would be maybe some slightly different composition to focus on the texture a bit more...just for the challenge, though.  As a portrait I like it just the way it is.</td>', 'Wow..hard to believe this one came in so low.  I think it''s just an excellent shot.  Good exposure, good focus and use of b/w and nice casual pose of the subject.  I like the rather dark contrast and tend to use that a bit more myself.  I think it adds some drama to a shot. It''s done really well here without overdoing it. The only thing I can see to do differently would be maybe some slightly different composition to focus on the texture a bit more...just for the challenge, though.  As a portrait I like it just the way it is.', '2005-08-03 23:59:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1587684, 205294, 6900, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by heida:</b></div><hr/><i> If anyone is interested I have put up spot edited version <a href="//www.deviantart.com/view/21064402/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How about an out of camera original?</td>', 'Originally posted by heida: If anyone is interested I have put up spot edited version here   How about an out of camera original?', '2005-08-04 22:30:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1588543, 206402, 36231, '<td valign="top">So, you''ve heard over and over again about the DOF.  I have to agree.  I love the textures, and the colors, but the POF is confusing.  Again, try different angles and apertures and use the one you look and like the best.  That doesn''t mean everyone else likes it, but you know you''ve posted a photo that touches you.</td>', 'So, you''ve heard over and over again about the DOF.  I have to agree.  I love the textures, and the colors, but the POF is confusing.  Again, try different angles and apertures and use the one you look and like the best.  That doesn''t mean everyone else likes it, but you know you''ve posted a photo that touches you.', '2005-08-05 10:41:37.000000', NULL, 0),
