(1598561, 206328, 37719, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot!  The center of focus being the walnut helps.  Good detail.  DoF fits the shot nicely.  Lighting is nice - not too severe but not too dull either.  A happy medium.  Well composed as well - not too distracting.  Nice job!</td>', 'Very nice shot!  The center of focus being the walnut helps.  Good detail.  DoF fits the shot nicely.  Lighting is nice - not too severe but not too dull either.  A happy medium.  Well composed as well - not too distracting.  Nice job!', '2005-08-09 20:04:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1601533, 203754, 34659, '<td valign="top">LOL @ your explanation of getting the shot.  I like this a lot.  The feather in the frog''s mouth is really great.  The DOF, sharpness, and composition are all good.  I''m surprised this didn''t do better in the challenge (although 5.2 ain''t bad in that challenge!).  Nice work (and hope you''ve recovered from your swim...)  ;-)</td>', 'LOL @ your explanation of getting the shot.  I like this a lot.  The feather in the frog''s mouth is really great.  The DOF, sharpness, and composition are all good.  I''m surprised this didn''t do better in the challenge (although 5.2 ain''t bad in that challenge!).  Nice work (and hope you''ve recovered from your swim...)  ;-)', '2005-08-10 15:37:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1602363, 206564, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jutilda:</b></div><hr/><i> I think the look you obtain when you sharpen something after the fact is never as good as if it were crystal clear to begin with.  I have found that more times than I care to mention.  Since you had asked in the forum, I thought I''d just respond this way. <br/> <br/>I love the single claw and the statement it makes as sort of an "alien" type prehistoric being, but to me it is still slightly out of focus.The lighting and composition is excellent  I hope this is helpful. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Just came across this comment. You are absolutely right and very helpful. Thanks a bunch.</td>', 'Originally posted by Jutilda: I think the look you obtain when you sharpen something after the fact is never as good as if it were crystal clear to begin with.  I have found that more times than I care to mention.  Since you had asked in the forum, I thought I''d just respond this way.  I love the single claw and the statement it makes as sort of an "alien" type prehistoric being, but to me it is still slightly out of focus.The lighting and composition is excellent  I hope this is helpful.   Just came across this comment. You are absolutely right and very helpful. Thanks a bunch.', '2005-08-10 21:10:39.000000', NULL, 0),
