(1698260, 206524, 19010, '<td valign="top">I just went browsing through my 10''s to refresh my memory and what my top votes had been on. There on the top of the list is this photo. 5.6??? I thought this was a good enough shot to get one of the 32 10''s I had given out since becoming a member. I must admit I never expected this one to score quite so low. Not a bad score, but I still thought this one would go a bit higher.</td>', 'I just went browsing through my 10''s to refresh my memory and what my top votes had been on. There on the top of the list is this photo. 5.6??? I thought this was a good enough shot to get one of the 32 10''s I had given out since becoming a member. I must admit I never expected this one to score quite so low. Not a bad score, but I still thought this one would go a bit higher.', '2005-09-12 09:41:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1702948, 206166, 37005, '<td valign="top">Great pic.  Too bad about the DQ.</td>', 'Great pic.  Too bad about the DQ.', '2005-09-13 09:13:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1708988, 204145, 16106, '<td valign="top">i like the framing and the lighting, but the greatest drama of the shot is where the light fades off the carving and you placed that all the way down in the bottom, I wish I could watch that fading more easily. As to the grain, Im not sure if that is grain in the object photographed, or an artifact of sharpening, but most voters here are very sensative to overshapening, and will sadly assume anything that looks like too much USM was applied, must be that, rather than assuming it to be inherent in the subject.<br/>The colors are great , but the focus is just a bit soft, but for the softness this is a very nice shot.</td>', 'i like the framing and the lighting, but the greatest drama of the shot is where the light fades off the carving and you placed that all the way down in the bottom, I wish I could watch that fading more easily. As to the grain, Im not sure if that is grain in the object photographed, or an artifact of sharpening, but most voters here are very sensative to overshapening, and will sadly assume anything that looks like too much USM was applied, must be that, rather than assuming it to be inherent in the subject.The colors are great , but the focus is just a bit soft, but for the softness this is a very nice shot.', '2005-09-14 15:58:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1711731, 203368, 28710, '<td valign="top">Well I think Canon deserves most of the credit on this one. Auto settings. Macro button pressed. Shutter snapped.<br/> <br/>Nice flower.<br/> <br/>Too bad you couldn''t have taken the time to control that little lighting issue that put all the distracting shadows all through the picture. Or perhaps you didn''t know how to do that.<br/> <br/>I thought you might appreciate some quality critical opines about your pic. After all, you know better than most that it''s the photographer that makes the picture, not the camera. Right?</td>', 'Well I think Canon deserves most of the credit on this one. Auto settings. Macro button pressed. Shutter snapped. Nice flower. Too bad you couldn''t have taken the time to control that little lighting issue that put all the distracting shadows all through the picture. Or perhaps you didn''t know how to do that. I thought you might appreciate some quality critical opines about your pic. After all, you know better than most that it''s the photographer that makes the picture, not the camera. Right?', '2005-09-15 14:59:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1724515, 203447, 37544, '<td valign="top">This picture shows great texture, it would have been better if the chives in the front of the image where in focus, IMO. I have noticed in your other pictures that you try to capture your subjects with interesting agles. I like that.</td>', 'This picture shows great texture, it would have been better if the chives in the front of the image where in focus, IMO. I have noticed in your other pictures that you try to capture your subjects with interesting agles. I like that.', '2005-09-20 17:01:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1728577, 203538, 39349, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful shot IMO. I love the textures on the glass and contrast of color. Lighting is dead on girl! I would have given this an 8 or higher if I were to vote on it for sure!</td>', 'This is a beautiful shot IMO. I love the textures on the glass and contrast of color. Lighting is dead on girl! I would have given this an 8 or higher if I were to vote on it for sure!', '2005-09-21 20:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
